course: dictionary
lesson: 10410
title: Trigger: a cause that starts something
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A trigger is the small lever you pull on a gun or tool to make it work, like the trigger on a water pistol or spray bottle. As a verb, to trigger something means to make it start or happen.
explain: Trigger also means a cause of a reaction. «Colds often trigger asthma» means a cold can make asthma start. Ask yourself: what happens next? The trigger is the thing that sets it off.
explain: Set off and cause are close friends of trigger. «Smoke triggers a smoke alarm» means smoke sets the alarm off. To check, swap in "sets off": if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
fact: A trigger is the small lever you pull to make a gun or tool work, like a water pistol or spray bottle.
fact: Never touch a real gun; tell an adult straight away.
fact: To trigger something means to make it start or happen.
fact: «A Venus flytrap shuts in about a tenth of a second when its trigger hairs are touched twice within about 20 seconds.»
fact: «Eating fast, fizzy drinks or a full stomach can trigger a hiccup.»
exercise: «Smoke triggers a smoke alarm.» What does triggers mean here? | Paints the alarm | *Makes the alarm start | Hides the alarm
exercise: On a water pistol, what is the trigger? | *The small lever you squeeze to make it squirt | The string that holds it | The coloured cap on the end | The bag it comes in
exercise: «A Venus flytrap shuts when its trigger hairs are touched twice within about 20 seconds.» Why is one touch, like a raindrop, not enough? | *Because it takes two touches within about 20 seconds to trigger the shut | Because flytraps cannot feel anything at all | Because raindrops are too small to see | Because the trap is always shut
test: What does it mean to trigger something? | To paint it bright red | To stop it for ever | *To make it start or happen
test: «Colds often trigger asthma.» Which word means the same as trigger here? | Cure | Forget | *Set off
exam: Ayesha reads «Pollen can trigger asthma» and asks what trigger means. Which answer is best? | To breathe in very slowly | *To cause asthma to start | To make pollen sweet | To remove pollen from the air
